Check 3: allow-scripts policy
-----------------------------
video/storytime-song/package.json line 34 holds allowScripts {"esbuild": false}.
git show c40b6b6f of the same file holds allowScripts {'esbuild': False}.
The phase diff of package.json contains 0 lines matching allowScripts.
npm reports in audit-after-d2-video.err: "allow-scripts .npmrc allow-scripts
setting is being ignored because package.json declares its own allowScripts
field". That message proves npm reads and applies the package.json field.
The esbuild entry denies the only install script, so the EALLOWSCRIPTS
workaround did not open a path for a blocked script to run. The structural
answer to the brief is: no install script that the policy blocks was added
or permitted, because the only candidate stayed denied and unchanged.
Evidence limit: Green's npm debug logs rotated out of ~/.npm/_logs before I
arrived, so I could not read the install log line by line. I record that as
a gap, not as a pass claim about log content.

